The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
old = i915_gem_active_raw(&vma->last_active, &vma->vm->i915->drm.struct_mutex);
active = kmalloc(sizeof(*active), GFP_KERNEL);
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the `kmalloc` function can invoke the shrinker, which may retire the `vma->last_active` request while the system is processing a new `i915_vma_move_to_active()` operation. If `vma->last_active` is retired, the bookkeeping for active instances becomes invalid, leading to potential access of a retired request.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (unlikely(!i915_gem_active_raw(&vma->last_active, &vma->vm->i915->drm.struct_mutex))) {
    kfree(active);
    goto out;
}
```
Reason:
This fix checks if `vma->last_active` is still valid after the potential invocation of the shrinker. If it is not valid (i.e., it has been retired), the newly allocated `active` instance is freed, preventing any further operations on an invalid request and ensuring the integrity of the bookkeeping.

